cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software record and the preprint below."
type: software
title: "AeroRec: an oracle-based diagnosis platform for bias propagation and debiasing boundaries in recommender systems"
abstract: >-
  AeroRec is a travel-recommendation platform built as a measurement instrument rather than a
  leaderboard entry. It implements a four-way recall → DeepFM ranking → five-step mixing pipeline
  with a graceful-degradation path, and wraps it in an oracle-based diagnostic harness in which the
  true CTR and the exposure propensity are known in closed form. That construction makes two
  questions answerable that production logs cannot answer: how exposure bias propagates through the
  recall / ranking / mixing stages, and under what conditions inverse-propensity-scoring debiasing
  costs more variance than the bias it removes. All reported numbers are regenerated from the
  committed result JSONs by scripts in this repository, and re-checked in CI by
  scripts/audit_paper_numbers.py against the manuscript's reported values.
